Tier 2 -- committed config corpora.

Each <name>.conf is a config file. Beside it:

  <name>.expected   the exact output of conf_dump after loading it
  <name>.check      the exact output of conf_check after loading it
  <name>.errors     the exact stderr of conf_load, for a file that must NOT
                    parse. A corpus has either .expected + .check, or .errors,
                    never both.

The paths in .errors are written with the placeholder CONF instead of the
temporary path the test copies the file to, because the message format
("<file>:<line>: <message>") is part of the contract and the directory is not.
